  "scope": "Real PM coordination on isolated copies of completed QA projects. No new worker/artifact completion is claimed; prior end-to-end evidence is issue 46. No API/fake fallback.",
  "engineeringTarget": "A durably saved same-author plain chat correction must release an obsolete call without awaiting its provider timeout. Deterministic regression requires completion within 1000ms.",
  "comparison": "Identical stalled-provider regression fails on baseline and passes after the fix. Live samples are observations, not a controlled wall-clock before/after speedup or provider comparison.",
  "limitations": [
    "External provider completion latency remains; unrelated ordered work can still queue behind necessary model work.",
    "Claude buffered JSON exposes first_output, not model first token. Network and remote computation cannot be separated.",
    "Codex uses the CLI default model; its resolved model ID is not exposed in these timing logs. Claude requested claude-sonnet-5.",
    "Initial harness failures (wrong combobox label; exact PM text excluded its badge) are preserved. No product failure was hidden.",
    "issue47 and issue47-live completedScreenAt is an API idle poll, not a DOM timestamp. Visible new PM answers are confirmed by screenshots; screenshot file completion is only an upper bound.",
    "issue47-final records composer-clear UI reaction. Repeated identical requests correctly produced no duplicate PM speech, so its completion is idle processing, not a new visible answer.",
    "No runtime configuration, process or folder in task-2/ensemble-benchmark was accessed or modified."
